en-US.description:
(Informal, addressee-lowering) Final endings used to:   
1. ask a guess about what follows if the preceding statement is true;   
2. indicate an expected result does not actually occur;   
3. invite the listener to guess;   
4. give a reason for the preceding sentence;   
5. ask the listener’s intention.

### Word information

ending · unspecified

